1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,442
Tick-Primed Hypersensitivity in Cosmetic and Aesthetic Procedures.

2
00:00:04,562 --> 00:00:09,240
Marielle He, Jordan Kai Simmons, and Babak Azizzadeh.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,113
Screen. Substitute. Prevent.

4
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:31,111
Alpha-gal syndrome, or A-G-S, is an acquired immunoglobulin E, or I-G-E–mediated, allergy to galactose-alpha-1,3-galactose in non-primate mammalian tissue and products. Diagnosis requires compatible history plus alpha-gal I-G-E. Sensitized does not equal reactive.

5
00:00:31,231 --> 00:00:42,924
The established pathway is tick-induced alpha-gal I-G-E reacting to a later mammalian exposure; a hypothesized product-associated sensitization pathway remains unestablished.

6
00:00:43,044 --> 00:00:58,829
The C-D-C identified 90,018 suspected U.S. cases from 2017 through 2022, and estimated 96,000 to 450,000 affected since 2010. Seropositivity is not clinical disease.

7
00:00:58,949 --> 00:01:22,335
Six steps. One: history. Two: confirm history plus alpha-gal I-G-E. Three: audit products. Four: verify species, source, formulation, and lot. Five: substitute source-verified hyaluronic acid, or H-A, or non-gelatin options. Six: allergy input when risk is material, plus epinephrine readiness.

8
00:01:22,455 --> 00:01:35,901
Oral exposure is delayed three to six hours. Parenteral may be immediate. Implants can prolong exposure. Food-challenge thresholds do not establish product safety.

9
00:01:36,021 --> 00:01:51,222
Porcine unfractionated heparin, or U-F-H: high-dose intravenous cardiac exposure caused severe reactions in 4 of 17 patients, or 24 percent. Heparin is not an absolute contraindication.

10
00:01:51,342 --> 00:02:12,389
Gelatin hemostats: demonstrated. Porcine heparin: clinical signal. Mammalian matrices: mechanistic, with no prospective cosmetic or aesthetic cohort. Collagen P-M-M-A and catgut: theoretical. Source-verified H-A, calcium hydroxylapatite, poly-L-lactic acid, or P-L-L-A, and lidocaine: no established A-G-S-specific risk.

11
00:02:12,509 --> 00:02:21,279
No prospective cosmetic or aesthetic cohort, validated procedure-specific screening threshold, or brand-level alpha-gal assay exists.

12
00:02:21,399 --> 00:02:34,410
This narration is decision support for licensed clinicians, not medical advice. Premedication does not reliably prevent anaphylaxis. Narrated by Marielle He. End of narration.
